  "result": "I implemented `satisfies(version, range)` in `src/semver.js` following `docs/SPEC.md`. `npm test` passes (3 tests, 0 failed).\n\nThe new tests are in `test/semver.test.js`. They cover the spec's comparator, X-range, tilde, caret, hyphen, prerelease and `||` examples. They also check that invalid versions and ranges return `false` instead of throwing. I only ran the checks in that file, and I didn't commit anything.\n\nThe spec doesn't cover a few cases, so I picked behaviour for them:\n- **`>*` and `<*`:** these match nothing.\n- **`>=*` and `<=*`:** these match any non-prerelease version.\n- **Capital `V`:** a leading `V` is rejected; only lowercase `v` is allowed.\n- **Prerelease on a partial version:** `1.x-beta` is invalid.\n- **Leading zeros in prerelease identifiers:** these are accepted, because the spec only restricts the major, minor and patch numbers.",
